A.kW.prototype={
ak(){return new A.uY(A.b(["\ud83c\udf3c Chapter 1: When the Game Began\n\nOnce upon a time, in the quiet corners of a chaotic game called PIMD back in 2012, two souls kept bumping into each other. You, the flower, quietly blooming in a pixel world, and me, a bee buzzing with curiosity. It started with simple chats, accidental taps, playful flirting. But it didn\u2019t stay simple for long.\n\nBefore we knew it, we were logging in not for the game, but for each other.\n\nIn between the avatars, club walls, and RP chaos, something real began. We talked about things we\u2019d never said aloud to anyone else. Somehow, it was easy. So easy it scared me sometimes.\n\nWe didn\u2019t just meet \u2014 we collided.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s a curious thing\u2026 how strangers become everything.\u201d\n\nBy March 25, 2012, we weren\u2019t just friends anymore. That was the first time I felt it \u2014 the beginning of us.",'\ud83c\udf3c Chapter 2: Outside the Game\n\nThe game slowly became background noise. We had outgrown it, but not each other. So we stepped out.\n\nTexts. Calls. Sleepy \u201cgood morning\u201d and \u201care you home safe?\u201d messages.\n\nWe\u2019d talk about life, work, and the most random things. When she couldn\u2019t bring her phone into work, she emailed me \u2014 updates, silly thoughts, little rants about annoying coworkers and bosses. I\u2019d wait for those emails like they were love letters.\n\nAt night, even when tired, we\u2019d still call \u2014 sometimes just to fall asleep with each other\u2019s presence still hanging in the air.\n\n"Even in silence, you felt close \u2014 like home sitting quietly beside me."\n\nWe were young, but somehow, it felt solid. Like we had stumbled into something rare.',"\ud83c\udf3c Chapter 3: Falling and Finding Again\n\nLike most stories, we weren\u2019t perfect. There were fights, misunderstandings, stubbornness \u2014 especially mine. We had our first real break in 2013. It wasn\u2019t loud or dramatic. Just quiet distance, and the ache of something unfinished.\n\nBut the heart knows where it belongs.\n\nNot even a year later, 2014, we were back. Like gravity pulled us again. This time, we were more sure. Happier. Deeper.\n\n\u201cLove leaves a fingerprint. You can\u2019t wash it off \u2014 even with time.\u201d\n\nWe grew into each other. And that growth felt like peace.",'\ud83c\udf3c Chapter 4: The Sweet Years\n\nThese were the golden years. We didn\u2019t need anything extravagant \u2014 just each other\u2019s time, attention, and small daily joys.\n\nWe\u2019d talk throughout our workdays. I\u2019d wait for your shift to end just to hear how your day went. You\u2019d ask about my frustrations and listen even if you were tired. We cheered each other on like teammates in a game only we understood.\n\nSometimes we\u2019d fight. Not over big things. Just over silly stuff. But it never lasted long.\n\nWe were soft with each other. Gentle. Like best friends who knew each other\u2019s triggers and still stayed anyway.\n\n"Some souls meet again and again \u2014 not out of chance, but choice."',"\ud83c\udf3c Chapter 5: The Long Winter\n\nMarch 2017. Something cracked. Maybe we were both worn out. Maybe life was too loud.\n\nWe stopped. No more calls. No more late-night chats. Just\u2026 silence.\n\nBut the story didn\u2019t end there.\n\nWe still peeked in each other\u2019s lives, didn\u2019t we? A like here. A short message there. Sometimes we flirted. Sometimes we argued. But we never really disappeared. Not completely.\n\nWe became ghosts with history. But even ghosts whisper when the night is quiet enough.\n\n\u201cSome endings aren\u2019t endings at all \u2014 just long pauses between heartbeats.\u201d",'\ud83c\udf3c Chapter 6: January 2025 \u2013 The Return\n\nYears passed. We dated others. Lived our separate lives. But something always felt missing \u2014 like no one quite got us the way we got each other.\n\nAnd then\u2026 January 2025.\n\nThe bee came back to the flower again.\n\nNot with grand declarations. Just a quiet \u201cHey\u201d that said more than any love letter. And slowly, we let the garden bloom again.\n\nWe talked. Laughed. Held space. Grew closer. Fell in love \u2014 all over again.\n\n"You came back, and I realized\u2026 I had been waiting all this time."','\ud83c\udf3c Chapter 7: Now, and Always\n\nIt\u2019s August 2025. Our 7th monthsary since returning to each other. But this story isn\u2019t about dates. It\u2019s about everything in between.\n\nIt\u2019s about love that paused, but never gave up. About silly AI photos, late-night thoughts, deep talks, and laughing about the past.\n\nIt\u2019s about you, Venice \u2014 my Beebee. My Love.\n\n"You are my favorite what if\u2026 that turned into my most beautiful yes."\n\nNo matter how many seasons we go through, I\u2019ll keep coming back. Again and again.',"\u2728 This book will be never ending, and this journey started since Day 1, with you. \u2728"],t.s),A.a5x(),A.a5x())}}
